coverage={
 'systems':['CNS','Soft tissue and bone','Peripheral nerve','Pediatric embryonal','Eye and orbit'],
 'basis':'WHO fifth-edition structures for CNS, soft tissue/bone and eye/orbit; broad malignant families, with molecularly distinct CNS/round-cell sarcoma entities retained. Malignant behavior is not synonymous with high histologic grade.',
 'merged':['Medulloblastoma molecular groups are internal alternatives within one broad row.','Ependymoma anatomic/molecular entities are internal alternatives within one row; nonmalignant subependymoma and myxopapillary ependymoma are excluded.','Liposarcoma, rhabdomyosarcoma, chondrosarcoma, osteosarcoma and chordoma histologic subsets are listed within broad rows.','Soft tissue, bone and visceral presentations of the same sarcoma family are combined, except when site changes molecular identity.','Peripheral neuroblastoma and ganglioneuroblastoma are combined.'],
 'excluded':['Benign and intermediate tumors: ordinary schwannoma/neurofibroma, grade 1–2 meningioma, pilocytic astrocytoma, most low-grade glioneuronal tumors, desmoid fibromatosis, ordinary giant cell tumor of bone, angiomatoid fibrous histiocytoma, conventional inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor, pseudomyogenic hemangioendothelioma, and other intermediate vascular/fibroblastic entities.','Provisional CNS DGONC, cribriform neuroepithelial tumor, FET::CREB intracranial mesenchymal tumor and desmoplastic myxoid pineal tumor are not automatically treated as established malignant entities.','CNS/ocular lymphomas and histiocytic neoplasms are covered with hematolymphoid tumors. CNS germ-cell tumors, renal embryonal tumors, GIST, epithelial/melanocytic skin/conjunctival tumors, salivary/lacrimal carcinomas and pituitary malignancies are covered in their respective organ families.'],
 'limitations':['This is an educational broad-family crosswalk, not a verbatim WHO taxonomy or an exhaustive list of every reported genomic alteration.','Evidence for exceptionally rare sarcomas may be limited to small cohorts; candidate findings are labeled and no fixed prevalence is implied.','Molecular grouping evolves; WHO5 emerging/provisional categories and behavior-code differences need explicit contextual interpretation.','A mutation, amplification, fusion or immunostain rarely proves tumor type without histology and clinical context.']
}
